{"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"title":"Sessions","modules":[{"name":"Sessions"}],"externalID":"Sessions","role":"collection","symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/Events\/Enricher\/sessions(timeout:kinds:file:fileID:function:line:column:)","doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/Events\/Enricher\/sessions(checkedTimeout:kinds:file:fileID:function:line:column:)","doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionEventKind","doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/NonPositiveSessionTimeout"],"anchor":"Putting-events-in-sessions","title":"Putting events in sessions"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionKey"],"anchor":"Reading-a-records-session","title":"Reading a record’s session"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionStarted","doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionEnded"],"anchor":"Session-events","title":"Session events"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/Trackers\/Sampler\/sessions(where:rate:)"],"anchor":"Sampling-whole-sessions","title":"Sampling whole sessions"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Sessions are opt-in. Add the sessions enricher to the ones a tracker is built with, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tracker’s worker sets each record’s ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionKey"},{"text":" to its session’s identifier. A session goes on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"while each event comes less than the timeout (30 minutes by default) after the one before it,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"measured between the records’ timestamps. The first event after a longer gap starts a new session.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The enricher tracks "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionStarted"},{"type":"text","text":" before each session’s first event, and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionEnded"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before that from the second session on, carrying the ended session’s duration. A run’s last session"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has no "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionEnded"},{"type":"text","text":": a session ends only when an event comes after the timeout. Pass "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kinds:"},{"type":"text","text":" to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"track only one kind of session event, or neither; every record still carries its key."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A session’s identifier is a version 7 UUID: the session’s start in Unix milliseconds, then random","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bits. It is held in the enricher’s memory only, never written to disk, and a new tracker, as on the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"next launch, starts a new session. Records a store kept from an earlier run carry no key.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sampler.sessions(rate:)"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps or drops every record of a session alike, its session events with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it, by the record’s "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionKey","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". It needs the sessions enricher among the tracker’s enrichers."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlin